WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:01.320
- It's no secret that we spend a lot

00:00:01.320 --> 00:00:03.540
of time and effort trying

00:00:03.540 --> 00:00:05.780
to appear confident on the surface

00:00:05.780 --> 00:00:07.800
when we're around other people

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:09.700
because we kind of have no choice.

00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:11.810
People are extremely judgmental

00:00:11.810 --> 00:00:13.360
whether they're aware of it or not.

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:16.460
Sizing people up is an
evolutionary mechanism.

00:00:16.460 --> 00:00:19.160
When we appear confident and self-assured,

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:21.470
people subconsciously place us higher

00:00:21.470 --> 00:00:23.020
on their social hierarchy.

00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:25.130
This is why it matters how you dress,

00:00:25.130 --> 00:00:26.960
the strength behind your voice

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:29.110
and your posture when you enter a room.

00:00:29.110 --> 00:00:31.640
All of these things
contribute tremendously

00:00:31.640 --> 00:00:33.710
to how people end up treating you.

00:00:33.710 --> 00:00:37.950
But the weird thing is so many
of us feel a huge disconnect

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:39.080
between the person

00:00:39.080 --> 00:00:42.140
that we're trying to
appear in the world as

00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:44.670
and who we actually are as a person

00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:48.050
because no matter how
meticulously we groom ourselves

00:00:48.050 --> 00:00:51.080
or how obsessively we keep
up with the latest trends,

00:00:51.080 --> 00:00:53.990
or how quip-y and clever
our manner of speech is,

00:00:53.990 --> 00:00:57.370
the whole thing ends up
feeling like a giant facade.

00:00:57.370 --> 00:00:59.400
Like we're just putting this show on,

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:01.090
we're not actually confident.

00:01:01.090 --> 00:01:02.770
We're slapping makeup on a pig.

00:01:02.770 --> 00:01:03.870
And this is a problem

00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:07.850
because the more you strain
to act like a confident person

00:01:07.850 --> 00:01:10.270
in the real world, people
don't really buy it.

00:01:10.270 --> 00:01:12.180
They can tell that it's forced.

00:01:12.180 --> 00:01:14.770
Fake smiles are really easy to spot.

00:01:14.770 --> 00:01:17.330
I think the reason why so many of us

00:01:17.330 --> 00:01:20.220
don't feel confident and rock solid

00:01:20.220 --> 00:01:22.440
is because we're forgetting a concept

00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:25.810
that is fundamental to the
way our psychology works.

00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:29.180
And that is that while we
are indeed very efficient

00:01:29.180 --> 00:01:31.750
at judging other people
and sizing them up,

00:01:31.750 --> 00:01:34.450
our brain uses the exact same mechanism

00:01:34.450 --> 00:01:36.100
to judge ourselves.

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:39.240
We are a fly on the wall of our own lives,

00:01:39.240 --> 00:01:41.750
constantly judging the things we say,

00:01:41.750 --> 00:01:43.460
the thoughts we entertain

00:01:43.460 --> 00:01:45.120
and the habits we indulge in.

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:47.750
And this constant observation happen

00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:49.730
without our conscious knowledge

00:01:49.730 --> 00:01:51.720
because it's subconscious knowledge.

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:53.440
And this subconscious of ours

00:01:53.440 --> 00:01:56.470
is always watching us, taking notes,

00:01:56.470 --> 00:01:59.640
comparing our lifestyle
to our value system.

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:01.610
And the longer time goes on,

00:02:01.610 --> 00:02:04.330
the more evidence our subconscious gathers

00:02:04.330 --> 00:02:06.630
to form an opinion about ourselves,

00:02:06.630 --> 00:02:08.660
just like it would with other people.

00:02:08.660 --> 00:02:10.780
So the more and more time we live

00:02:10.780 --> 00:02:13.270
in contradiction to our value system,

00:02:13.270 --> 00:02:15.910
the lower our opinion
will be of ourselves.

00:02:15.910 --> 00:02:19.110
So if we happen to have a
very low opinion of ourselves,

00:02:19.110 --> 00:02:22.850
we'd have very low self-esteem,
low self-confidence,

00:02:22.850 --> 00:02:25.490
low self-efficacy, then
there's a very good chance

00:02:25.490 --> 00:02:28.350
that your subconscious has
observed you live your life

00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:30.130
in a way that is contradictory

00:02:30.130 --> 00:02:32.200
to your fundamental value system.

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:35.210
And this is kind of what
affirmation culture gets wrong.

00:02:35.210 --> 00:02:37.050
You know, it sounds all well and good

00:02:37.050 --> 00:02:39.530
and helpful to look yourself in the mirror

00:02:39.530 --> 00:02:42.450
and say you are powerful
and you are strong.

00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:44.520
You are good looking, you attract wealth,

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:46.250
you attract women, you attract men,

00:02:46.250 --> 00:02:47.100
you attract everyone.

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:50.440
But the truth is your
subconscious is harder to fool.

00:02:50.440 --> 00:02:52.170
If you look yourself in the mirror

00:02:52.170 --> 00:02:55.460
and say one thing and then
behave the opposite way,

00:02:55.460 --> 00:02:57.620
your subconscious isn't fooled.

00:02:57.620 --> 00:02:58.940
It watched you do that.

00:02:58.940 --> 00:03:01.310
It'll say wow, this guy never does

00:03:01.310 --> 00:03:02.510
what he says he's gonna do.

00:03:02.510 --> 00:03:04.150
I'm gonna use this information

00:03:04.150 --> 00:03:06.270
to develop a self-doubt complex

00:03:06.270 --> 00:03:08.520
that will leak into every area of his life

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:11.370
and his interactions with
others, especially women.

00:03:11.370 --> 00:03:12.920
And that's the insidious thing

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:14.280
about our subconscious.

00:03:14.280 --> 00:03:16.970
It influences our mood, our mindset

00:03:16.970 --> 00:03:19.490
and our overall mental state far more

00:03:19.490 --> 00:03:21.080
than we probably realize

00:03:21.080 --> 00:03:23.220
and that's because our
subconscious accounts

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:26.820
for over 90% of our
overall mental function.

00:03:26.820 --> 00:03:31.300
So how we conduct ourself in
its presence is everything.

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:32.690
So needless to say,

00:03:32.690 --> 00:03:34.820
the key to confidence in life,

00:03:34.820 --> 00:03:38.520
the key to feeling self-assured
is not to double down

00:03:38.520 --> 00:03:41.440
and care more about what
other people think of you,

00:03:41.440 --> 00:03:44.440
it's to take more
seriously this relationship

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:46.670
that you have with your own subconscious.

00:03:46.670 --> 00:03:49.450
And to realize that you
can form a partnership

00:03:49.450 --> 00:03:51.790
and a friendship with your subconscious.

00:03:51.790 --> 00:03:53.580
And I know that sounds super woo-woo

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:55.370
and spiritual and you like what the (beep)

00:03:55.370 --> 00:03:56.460
is this guy talking about?

00:03:56.460 --> 00:03:59.890
But if you like the idea of
forming a better relationship

00:03:59.890 --> 00:04:01.590
with your own subconscious,

00:04:01.590 --> 00:04:02.810
then a great way to do that

00:04:02.810 --> 00:04:05.120
is to develop that relationship

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:06.950
like you would any other relationship:

00:04:06.950 --> 00:04:09.390
by spending time to get
to know the other person.

00:04:09.390 --> 00:04:11.660
You need to spend time
to get to know yourself,

00:04:11.660 --> 00:04:15.050
to uncover what your
fundamental value system is

00:04:15.050 --> 00:04:17.910
so that you can better
live in accordance to that.

00:04:17.910 --> 00:04:21.268
So take some time to ask
yourself some key questions.

00:04:21.268 --> 00:04:23.300
Take out a pen and paper,

00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:26.090
and ask yourself what
kind of person do I want

00:04:26.090 --> 00:04:27.160
to be in this world?

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:29.160
How can I live my life in a way

00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:30.710
that I would be proud of?

00:04:30.710 --> 00:04:33.790
What kind of habits
does my ideal self have?

00:04:33.790 --> 00:04:35.860
And if I was my ideal self,

00:04:35.860 --> 00:04:38.230
how would I interact with
the people around me?

00:04:38.230 --> 00:04:40.990
How would I spend my time
when nobody is around?

00:04:40.990 --> 00:04:43.800
Does my ideal self make
mistakes sometimes?

00:04:43.800 --> 00:04:46.640
If so, how does my ideal self respond

00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:47.830
to the mistakes I make?

00:04:47.830 --> 00:04:50.890
Would I learn from them and
encourage myself to do better?

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:53.504
Your answers to these types of questions

00:04:53.504 --> 00:04:55.640
will help you uncover truths

00:04:55.640 --> 00:04:57.350
that you hold about yourself

00:04:57.350 --> 00:05:00.780
and the standards that you're
trying to uphold yourself to

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:01.910
because whether you're aware

00:05:01.910 --> 00:05:04.150
of these ideals consciously or not,

00:05:04.150 --> 00:05:05.990
they're there in your subconscious,

00:05:05.990 --> 00:05:09.290
and your subconscious is
constantly comparing your behavior

00:05:09.290 --> 00:05:10.620
to these ideals.

00:05:10.620 --> 00:05:12.830
So it's super important to take some time

00:05:12.830 --> 00:05:16.130
to try to figure out
what constitutes a good

00:05:16.130 --> 00:05:18.770
and honorable person according to you.

00:05:18.770 --> 00:05:20.820
And chances are there's a lot of truth

00:05:20.820 --> 00:05:22.660
to these underlying beliefs.

00:05:22.660 --> 00:05:25.290
And sometimes these
beliefs are a little skewed

00:05:25.290 --> 00:05:26.670
and they need correcting,

00:05:26.670 --> 00:05:28.780
and you need to form healthier values

00:05:28.780 --> 00:05:30.970
and healthier expectations of yourself.

00:05:30.970 --> 00:05:32.070
So a great way to do this

00:05:32.070 --> 00:05:33.800
is to go through this whole process

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:34.960
of writing this stuff down,

00:05:34.960 --> 00:05:36.700
and diving deep by yourself,

00:05:36.700 --> 00:05:38.450
and then taking that information

00:05:38.450 --> 00:05:40.600
to a friend or a third party,

00:05:40.600 --> 00:05:43.230
preferably a therapist or a
mental health professional

00:05:43.230 --> 00:05:46.190
and try to figure out whether
or not this value system

00:05:46.190 --> 00:05:48.360
is actually useful for you.

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:51.810
Are you holding yourself
to unrealistic expectations

00:05:51.810 --> 00:05:54.240
or are these healthy
and good ideals to have?

00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:56.490
Because either way, there's
no getting around the fact

00:05:56.490 --> 00:05:59.400
that if you want to develop a
better opinion about yourself,

00:05:59.400 --> 00:06:02.250
your behaviors and your
values need to match.

00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:03.930
And in order for that to happen,

00:06:03.930 --> 00:06:05.750
either your behaviors need to change

00:06:05.750 --> 00:06:07.500
or your values need to change.

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:09.270
As you go through this process,

00:06:09.270 --> 00:06:12.690
you'll probably realize that
you are on your own side more

00:06:12.690 --> 00:06:14.260
than you probably realize.

00:06:14.260 --> 00:06:15.530
And when your conscious mind

00:06:15.530 --> 00:06:18.299
and your subconscious
mind is on the same page,

00:06:18.299 --> 00:06:21.470
you'll find that there's
a certain uniformity

00:06:21.470 --> 00:06:22.380
to your character.

00:06:22.380 --> 00:06:24.480
You don't say one thing
and then do another.

00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:26.090
You don't act one way in public

00:06:26.090 --> 00:06:28.000
and then act another way in private.

00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:30.530
You'll be a more consistent human being

00:06:30.530 --> 00:06:32.900
with a more authentic identity.

00:06:32.900 --> 00:06:35.000
You'll feel like yourself.

00:06:35.000 --> 00:06:36.810
You'll feel like you're more you.

00:06:36.810 --> 00:06:39.450
And that's a really
intangible thing to try

00:06:39.450 --> 00:06:41.210
to relay to you

00:06:41.210 --> 00:06:43.050
but it is a very real feeling.

00:06:43.050 --> 00:06:46.020
And that feeling is what
confidence feels like.

00:06:46.020 --> 00:06:48.110
It's to be unapologetically you

00:06:48.110 --> 00:06:49.680
in the presence of others,

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:52.150
while you're alone, it
just doesn't really matter.

00:06:52.150 --> 00:06:54.730
You're you no matter the circumstances.

00:06:54.730 --> 00:06:57.370
And I really hope that this
video gives you some ideas

00:06:57.370 --> 00:06:59.943
as to how you can get there in your life.

